==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Wildberry}}
{{Quests|
{{BotW Quest
 |name= The Mystery Polluter
 |type= Side Quest
 |giver= [[Dalia]]
 |location= [[Gerudo Town]]
}}
}}
Wildberries are found growing on bushes in the [[Gerudo Highlands]] and [[Hebra Mountains]],<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> or they can be dropped by [[Hinox]]es when defeated. They can be eaten raw to restore half of a [[Life Gauge|Heart]]. If a Wildberry is roasted over a [[Campfire]] or dropped in a hot location like [[Death Mountain]], it becomes a [[Roasted Wildberry]], which doubles its healing properties to heal a full Heart of the Life Gauge. At the [[Kochi Dye Shop]], Wildberries are one of the ingredients that can make [[Peach Dye]]. Wildberries are not required to upgrade any pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]].

As part of the [[Side Quest]] "[[The Mystery Polluter]]," [[Link]] must give [[Calyban]] 10 Wildberries in order to get her to stop polluting the [[Water (Terrain)|Water]] trough in [[Dalia]]'s garden.<ref name="BotW Calyban"/><ref name="BotW Calyban 2"/> Once Link delivers the Wildberries, Calyban will help [[Dalia]] start a Wildberry garden in [[Gerudo Town]], which completes the Side Quest.<ref name="BotW Calyban 3"/>

Wildberries are necessary to make a [[Wildberry Crepe]] in a [[Cooking Pot]]. Either a Wildberry or an [[Apple]] is needed to make [[Fruitcake]].
